From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: make usb3_phy_gdsc a child of usb30_prim_gdsc

The USB/DP combo PHY's aux, com_aux and pipe clock branches sit in the
USB30 core block (0x39060, 0x39064, 0x39068), gated by usb30_prim_gdsc,
while the PHY's own power domain is usb3_phy_gdsc. PortareOS lets the
dwc3 glue runtime-suspend (udev 81-usb-runtime-pm.rules), which drops
usb30_prim_gdsc. A DisplayPort connector probe then initialises the
PHY with those branches unpowered:

  gcc_usb3_prim_phy_aux_clk status stuck at 'off'
  Failed to enable clk 'aux': -16
  phy phy-88e8000.phy.3: phy init failed --> -16

seen on the Retroid Pocket Nova from modetest at a game launch. With
usb3_phy_gdsc a subdomain of usb30_prim_gdsc, gdsc_register() links
them and powering the PHY powers the core block for as long as the PHY
is in use; the USB runtime saving stays for the rest of the time.
---

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3072,6 +3072,12 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb3_phy_gdsc",
 	},
+	/*
+	 * The combo PHY's aux, com_aux and pipe clock branches live in the
+	 * USB30 core block, so initialising the PHY for DisplayPort while the
+	 * USB controller is runtime-suspended leaves them stuck off.
+	 */
+	.parent = &usb30_prim_gdsc.pd,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
